        "change_category": "guard",
        "intent_summary": "Adds overflow validation for received subvolume UUID insertion to prevent transaction aborts and protect against denial-of-service exploitation.",
        "what": "Added a comparison between root_item->received_uuid and sa->uuid using memcmp(), followed by a conditional call to btrfs_uuid_tree_check_overflow() before attempting to add the UUID to the tree. If overflow would occur, the function returns early via goto out.",
        "how": "Prevents transaction aborts by validating UUID tree space availability before attempting insertion. This avoids -EOVERFLOW errors that would trigger transaction rollback and potentially leave the filesystem in read-only mode, blocking a denial-of-vector attack."
      }
